<!doctype html><html lang=en dir=ltr><head><meta charset=utf-8><title>Apertus 1.0 - Apertus</title><meta name=viewport content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name=description content="A fully open, transparent, multilingual language model"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Apertus News"><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:url" content="https://apertus-ai.org/articles/2025-09-apertus-1-0/"><meta property="og:title" content="Apertus 1.0"><meta property="og:description" content="A fully open, transparent, multilingual language model"><meta property="og:image" content="https://apertus-ai.org/articles/2025-09-apertus-1-0/csm_ETH_Apertus_Keyvisual_Final-LY2_keyvisual_04d728dd41.jpeg"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="Apertus 1.0"><meta name=twitter:card content="summary_large_image"><meta name=twitter:title content="Apertus 1.0"><meta name=twitter:description content="A fully open, transparent, multilingual language model"><meta name=twitter:image content="https://apertus-ai.org/articles/2025-09-apertus-1-0/csm_ETH_Apertus_Keyvisual_Final-LY2_keyvisual_04d728dd41.jpeg"><meta name=author content="Swiss AI Initiative"><meta name=website content="Apertus"><meta name=version content="v1.5"><link rel=icon href=/favicon/favicon.ico sizes=any><link rel=icon type=image/svg+xml href=/favicon/favicon.svg><link rel=apple-touch-icon sizes=180x180 href=/favicon/apple-touch-icon.png><link rel=icon type=image/png sizes=32x32 href=/favicon/favicon-32x32.png><link rel=icon type=image/png sizes=16x16 href=/favicon/favicon-16x16.png><link rel=manifest crossorigin=use-credentials href=/favicon/site.webmanifest><link rel=stylesheet href=/scss/style.min.b8cb4b2942479db7ee7f2cb2881d1928ba906f6eeb7a0c5398fbc8467b1242b466242fbd5a1fc561df82c01ee1cbd7e7.css integrity=sha384-uMtLKUJHnbfufyyyiB0ZKLqQb27regxTmPvIRnsSQrRmJC+9Wh/FYd+CwB7hy9fn><script src=/js/bootstrap.a247e6d1be5b223e2d6792fa0caefd034e310929998b92b2fef1dbae94692301f759af6c7ab43cd4789d797d0f956c14.js integrity=sha384-okfm0b5bIj4tZ5L6DK79A04xCSmZi5Ky/vHbrpRpIwH3Wa9serQ81HideX0PlWwU defer></script></head><body><div id=content><main><style>html{overflow-y:scroll!important}body{font-size:1.125rem;min-height:calc(100vh + 1px)}.nav-link{font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:500}p,li{line-height:1.75}.row.g-5{--bs-gutter-x:5rem}.nav-link{color:#374151!important;transition:color .2s ease}.nav-link:hover{color:#49bed8!important}.nav-link.active{color:#49bed8!important}#main-nav{z-index:100;transition:background-color .3s,box-shadow .3s;background-color:transparent;box-shadow:none}@media(max-width:991px){#main-nav{background-color:#fff;box-shadow:0 3px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.3)}}#main-nav.scrolled{background-color:rgba(255,255,255,.95);box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.1)}#nav-brand{opacity:0;pointer-events:none;transition:opacity .3s}#main-nav.scrolled #nav-brand{opacity:1;pointer-events:auto}</style><nav id=main-nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg position-fixed scrolled top-0 w-100"><div class=container-fluid style=max-width:1100px><a id=nav-brand class=navbar-brand href=/><img src=/images/apertvs.svg alt=Apertus style=max-width:95%;max-height:18px>
</a><button class="navbar-toggler border-0" type=button data-bs-toggle=collapse data-bs-target=#navbarNav aria-controls=navbarNav aria-expanded=false aria-label="Toggle navigation">
<span class=navbar-toggler-icon></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse justify-content-end" id=navbarNav><ul class="navbar-nav gap-4"><li class=nav-item><a class=nav-link href=/pages/get-started/>Get Started</a></li><li class=nav-item><a class=nav-link href=/pages/documentation/>Documentation</a></li><li class=nav-item><a class=nav-link href=/pages/research/>Research</a></li><li class=nav-item><a class=nav-link href=/pages/about/>About</a></li><li class=nav-item><a class=nav-link href=/contact/>Contact</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><header class="mb-8 mt-5 pt-5 pb-5"><div class=container style=max-width:900px><h1 class="text-4xl mb-4">Apertus 1.0</h1><img src=csm_ETH_Apertus_Keyvisual_Final-LY2_keyvisual_04d728dd41.jpeg alt="Apertus 1.0" class="w-100 h-96 object-cover rounded-lg mb-6"><div class="article-summary fs-4 m-4">A fully open, transparent, multilingual language model</div></div></header><a name=start-content></a><section class="page-content bg-white pb-5 mt-4"><div class=container style=max-width:900px><div class="fs-5 mr-4 mb-4">September 2, 2025</div><div class=content-body><h5 id=epfl-eth-zurich-and-cscs-released-apertus-today-switzerlands-first-large-scale-open-multilingual-language-model--a-milestone-in-generative-ai-for-transparency-and-diversity>EPFL, ETH Zurich and CSCS released Apertus today, Switzerland&rsquo;s first large-scale, open, multilingual language model &mdash; a milestone in generative AI for transparency and diversity.</h5><p>In July, EPFL, ETH Zurich, and CSCS announced their joint initiative to build a large language model (LLM). Now, this model is available and serves as a building block for developers and organisations for future applications such as chatbots, translation systems, or educational tools.</p><p>The model is named <a href=https://www.swiss-ai.org/apertus>Apertus</a> &ndash; Latin for &ldquo;open&rdquo; &ndash; highlighting its distinctive feature: the entire development process, including its architecture, model weights, and training data and recipes, is openly accessible and fully documented. </p><p>AI researchers, professionals, and experienced enthusiasts can either access the model through the strategic partner Swisscom or download it from <a href=https://huggingface.co/>Hugging Face</a> &ndash; a platform for AI models and applications &ndash; and deploy it for their own projects. Apertus is freely available in two sizes &ndash; featuring 8 billion and 70 billion parameters, the smaller model being more appropriate for individual usage. Both models are released under a permissive open-source license, allowing use in education and research as well as broad societal and commercial applications.</p><p><strong>A fully open-source LLM</strong></p><p>As a fully open language model, Apertus allows researchers, professionals and enthusiasts to build upon the model and adapt it to their specific needs, as well as to inspect any part of the training process. This distinguishes Apertus from models that make only selected components accessible.</p><p>&ldquo;With this release, we aim to provide a blueprint for how a trustworthy, sovereign, and inclusive AI model can be developed,&rdquo; says Martin Jaggi, Professor of Machine Learning at EPFL and member of the Steering Committee of the Swiss AI Initiative. The model will be regularly updated by the development team which includes specialized engineers and a large number of researchers from CSCS, ETH Zurich and EPFL. </p><p><strong>A driver of innovation</strong></p><p>With its open approach, EPFL, ETH Zurich and CSCS are venturing into new territory. &ldquo;Apertus is not a conventional case of technology transfer from research to product. Instead, we see it as a driver of innovation and a means of strengthening AI expertise across research, society and industry,&rdquo; says Thomas Schulthess, Director of CSCS and Professor at ETH Zurich. In line with their tradition, EPFL, ETH Zurich and CSCS are providing both foundational technology and infrastructure to foster innovation across the economy.</p><p>Trained on 15 trillion tokens across more than 1,000 languages &ndash; 40% of the data is non-English &ndash; Apertus includes many languages that have so far been underrepresented in LLMs, such as Swiss German, Romansh, and many others.</p><p>&ldquo;Apertus is built for the public good. It stands among the few fully open LLMs at this scale and is the first of its kind to embody multilingualism, transparency, and compliance as foundational design principles&rdquo;, says Imanol Schlag, technical lead of the LLM project and Research Scientist at ETH Zurich.</p><p>&ldquo;Swisscom is proud to be among the first to deploy this pioneering large language model on our sovereign Swiss AI Platform. As a strategic partner of the Swiss AI Initiative, we are supporting the access of Apertus during the Swiss {ai} Weeks. This underscores our commitment to shaping a secure and responsible AI ecosystem that serves the public interest and strengthens Switzerland&rsquo;s digital sovereignty&rdquo;, comments Daniel Dobos, Research Director at Swisscom. </p><p><strong>Accessibility</strong></p><p>While setting up Apertus is straightforward for professionals and proficient users, additional components such as servers, cloud infrastructure or specific user interfaces are required for practical use. The upcoming Swiss {ai} Weeks hackathons will be the first opportunity for developers to experiment hands-on with Apertus, test its capabilities, and provide feedback for improvements to future versions. </p><p>Swisscom will provide a dedicated interface to hackathon participants, making it easier to interact with the model. As of today, Swisscom business customers will be able to access the Apertus model via Swisscom&rsquo;s sovereign Swiss AI platform.</p><p>Furthermore, for people outside of Switzerland, the <a href=https://publicai.co>Public AI Inference Utility</a> will make Apertus accessible as part of a global movement for public AI. &ldquo;Currently, Apertus is the leading public AI model: a model built by public institutions, for the public interest. It is our best proof yet that AI can be a form of public infrastructure like highways, water, or electricity,&rdquo; says Joshua Tan, Lead Maintainer of the Public AI Inference Utility. </p><p><strong>Transparency and compliance</strong></p><p>Apertus is designed with transparency at its core, thereby ensuring full reproducibility of the training process. Alongside the models, the research team has published a range of resources: comprehensive documentation and source code of the training process and datasets used, model weights including intermediate checkpoints &ndash; all released under the permissive open-source license, which also allows for commercial use. The terms and conditions are available via Hugging Face.</p><p>Apertus was developed with due consideration to Swiss data protection laws, Swiss copyright laws, and the transparency obligations under the EU AI Act. Particular attention has been paid to data integrity and ethical standards: the training corpus builds only on data which is publicly available. It is filtered to respect machine-readable opt-out requests from websites, even retroactively, and to remove personal data, and other undesired content before training begins. </p><p><strong>The beginning of a journey</strong></p><p>&ldquo;Apertus demonstrates that generative AI can be both powerful and open,&rdquo; says Antoine Bosselut, Professor and Head of the Natural Language Processing Laboratory at EPFL and Co-Lead of the Swiss AI Initiative. &ldquo;The release of Apertus is not a final step, rather it&rsquo;s the beginning of a journey, a long-term commitment to open, trustworthy, and sovereign AI foundations, for the public good worldwide. We are excited to see developers engage with the model at the Swiss {ai} Weeks hackathons. Their creativity and feedback will help us to improve future generations of the model.&rdquo;</p><p>Future versions aim to expand the model family, improve efficiency, and explore domain-specific adaptations in fields like law, climate, health and education. They are also expected to integrate additional capabilities, while maintaining strong standards for transparency.</p><p><em>Image above: Apertus Key Visual (Image: EPFL, ETH Zurich, CSCS / molinari design)</em></p><h3 id=about-apertus-and-the-swiss-ai-initiative>About Apertus and the Swiss AI Initiative</h3><p>Apertus was developed as part of the <a href=https://www.swiss-ai.org>Swiss AI Initiative</a>, led by EPFL and ETH Zurich. It is the result of a collaborative effort bringing together researchers, engineers, and students from across Switzerland, alongside the engineers and infrastructure of the Swiss National Supercomputing Centre (CSCS). This collective expertise, spanning multiple institutions and disciplines, has made the development of Apertus possible.</p><h3 id=funding-and-strategic-partnerships>Funding and strategic partnerships</h3><p>The development of the large language model and the research into other domain-specific foundation models is funded by an investment of over 10 million GPU hours on &ldquo;Alps&rdquo; by CSCS, and by the ETH Board &ndash; the strategic management and supervisory body of the ETH Domain (comprising ETH Zurich, EPFL, WSL, PSI, Empa, and Eawag). This funding is complemented by contributions from strategic partners, most notably Swisscom, Switzerland&rsquo;s largest telecommunications provider.</p><h3 id=about-the-swiss-ai-weeks>About the Swiss {ai} Weeks</h3><p><a href=https://swiss-ai-weeks.ch>Swiss {ai} Weeks</a> is a collaborative initiative to turn Switzerland&rsquo;s groundbreaking AI research into societal and economic impact. Through hackathons, expert events, public engagement, and startup incubation, it connects researchers, developers, entrepreneurs, and citizens around a shared goal: shaping ethical, open, and trustworthy use of AI. At the heart of the effort is Switzerland&rsquo;s first open-source Large Language Model &ndash; developed with Swiss values in mind: transparency, responsibility and multilinguality. Swiss {ai} Weeks activates a collective push for responsible AI application &ndash; decentralised, hands-on, and built for the common good. The initiators of the initiative include EPFL AI Center, ETH AI Center, Swisscom, Impact Hub Switzerland, Kickstart Innovation, Panter, and Wildcard Media.</p><h3 id=related-articles>Related articles</h3><ul><li><a href=https://ethz.ch/en/news-and-events/eth-news/news/2025/07/a-language-model-built-for-the-public-good.html>A language model built for the public good | ETH Zurich</a></li><li><a href=https://ethz.ch/en/news-and-events/eth-news/news/2025/03/globe-vertrauenswuerdige-ki-verlaesslich-und-berechenbar.html>Trustworthy AI &ndash; reliable and predictable | ETH Zurich</a></li><li><a href=https://actu.epfl.ch/news/switzerland-and-ai-tiny-but-mighty/>Switzerland and AI: tiny but mighty - EPFL</a></li><li><a href=https://www.swisscom.ch/en/about/news/2025/05/14-vertrauenswuerdige-ki-entwicklung.html>AI development in Switzerland | Swisscom</a></li></ul></div></div></section><div class="social-icons text-center"><a title="Post on Mastodon" href="https://share.joinmastodon.org/#text=#Apertus+https%3a%2f%2fapertus-ai.org%2farticles%2f2025-09-apertus-1-0%2f" target=_blank rel=noopener class=icon-button><i class="bi bi-mastodon"></i><span></span></a>
<a title="Post on Hugging Face" href="https://huggingface.co/?post=true&url=https%3a%2f%2fapertus-ai.org%2farticles%2f2025-09-apertus-1-0%2f" target=_blank rel=noopener class=icon-button><i class="bi bi-emoji-laughing"></i><span></span></a>
<a title="Post on LinkedIn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?text=%23Apertus+https%3a%2f%2fapertus-ai.org%2farticles%2f2025-09-apertus-1-0%2f" target=_blank rel=noopener class=icon-button><i class="bi bi-linkedin"></i><span></span></a></div></main><style>.content-body h2{margin-top:2.5rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;color:#1a1a1a;text-align:center}.content-body h2:first-child{margin-top:0}.section-intro{color:#6b7280;margin-bottom:4rem;font-size:110%;text-align:center}.content-body p{color:#374151;margin-bottom:1.25rem}.content-body ul,.content-body ol{color:#374151;margin-bottom:1.5rem}.content-body li{margin-bottom:.75rem}.content-body a{color:rgba(var(--bs-link-color-rgb),var(--bs-link-opacity,1));text-decoration:none}.content-body a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.content-body a.btn-primary{color:#fff}.content-body strong{color:#1a1a1a}.content-body hr{margin:2.5rem 0;border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb}.content-body em{color:#6b7280}.content-body img{max-width:100%}.content-body blockquote{margin-left:.5em;padding-left:1em;border-left:1px solid grey;font-size:125%;opacity:.8}.content-body table{margin-bottom:2em}.content-body table th,.content-body table td{padding:1em 1em 0 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb}.card-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:1.5rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.card{display:block!important;flex-direction:unset!important;border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem;transition:box-shadow .2s,border-color .2s;text-align:center}.card:hover{border-color:#49bed8;box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,8%)}.card.card-grey{border-color:#d3d3d3!important;border-style:dashed}.card a{text-decoration:none}.card h4{margin:0 0 .5rem;color:#1a1a1a;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.4}.card p{margin:0 0 1rem;color:#6b7280;font-size:.95rem}.card .meta{font-size:.85rem;color:#9ca3af}.card .authors{color:#6b7280;font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:.75rem}.card-logo{height:32px!important;width:auto!important;margin-bottom:1rem;object-fit:contain}.card img:not(.card-logo){width:auto;max-width:100%;object-fit:contain}.card-logo.card-logo-left{float:left;margin-bottom:1em;margin-right:-32px}.badge{display:inline-block;width:auto;padding:.25rem .5rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:500;margin-right:.5rem;margin-bottom:.25rem;background:#fff;color:#999}.badge-free{background:#d1fae5;color:#065f46}.badge-swiss{background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b}.badge-partner{background:#dbeafe;color:#000}.badge-supported{background:#dbeafe;color:#1e40af}.faq-item{margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding:1.5rem;border:2px solid #c0c4cc;border-radius:12px}.faq-item:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.faq-item h4{margin:0 0 .5rem;color:#1a1a1a;font-size:1.1rem}.faq-item p{margin:0;color:#374151;line-height:1.6}.charter-meta{text-align:center;color:#6b7280;margin-bottom:2rem}.preamble{color:#374151;margin:1.5rem 0;line-height:1.7}.articles-list{background:#f8f9fa;border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem 1.5rem 1.5rem 2.5rem;margin:2rem 0}.articles-list li{margin-bottom:.5rem;color:#374151}.article{margin:2rem 0}.article h4{color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:.75rem}.article p{color:#374151;line-height:1.7}.icon-button{background-color:#fff;border-radius:3.6rem;cursor:pointer;display:inline-block;font-size:2rem;height:3.6rem;line-height:3.6rem;margin:0 5px;position:relative;text-align:center;-webkit-user-select:none;-moz-user-select:none;-ms-user-select:none;user-select:none;width:3.6rem}.icon-button span{background-color:#4099ff;border-radius:0;display:block;height:0;left:50%;margin:0;position:absolute;top:50%;-webkit-transition:all .3s;-moz-transition:all .3s;-o-transition:all .3s;transition:all .3s;width:0}.icon-button:hover span{width:3.6rem;height:3.6rem;border-radius:3.6rem;margin:-1.8rem}.icon-button:hover i{color:#fff}.icon-button i{background:0 0;color:#4099ff;height:3.6rem;left:0;line-height:3.6rem;position:absolute;transition:all .3s;width:3.6rem;z-index:10}.roadmap{margin:2rem 0 1rem}.roadmap-item{position:relative;padding:0 0 1.75rem 2.5rem}.roadmap-item::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:7px;top:20px;bottom:-4px;width:2px;background:#e5e7eb}.roadmap-item:last-child::before{display:none}.roadmap-item::after{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:4px;width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:#49bed8;border:3px solid #49bed8}.roadmap-item.planned::after{background:#fff;border-color:#c0c4cc}.roadmap-item.latest .roadmap-content{background:#f0f9fc;border:1px solid #49bed8;border-radius:12px;padding:1rem 1.25rem}.roadmap-header{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem}.roadmap-title{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:#1a1a1a}.roadmap-weights{font-size:.85rem;white-space:nowrap}.roadmap .badge-released{background:#d1fae5;color:#065f46}.roadmap .badge-latest{background:#dbeafe;color:#1e40af}.roadmap .badge-planned{background:#f3f4f6;color:#6b7280}.roadmap-item p{margin-bottom:0}.roadmap-item ul{margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem}.roadmap-item li{margin-bottom:.35rem}.roadmap-item li:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.roadmap-note{color:#9ca3af;font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:2.5rem}</style></div><footer class="footer mt-auto py-4 bg-light border-top"><div class=container><div class="row align-items-center"><div class=col-md-6><ul class="list-inline mb-0"><li class=list-inline-item><a href=/pages/legal/>Legal Notice</a></li></ul></div><div class="col-md-6 text-md-end"><span class=text-muted>© 2026 ETH AI Center & EPFL AI Center</span></div></div></div></footer><script src=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js></script><link rel=stylesheet href=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css></body></html>